id: regexp/text/m6-string-search/0001
area: regexp
op: String.prototype.search
in: str:"delete RegExp.prototype[Symbol.search]; \"abc\".search(/b/)"
out: error: TypeError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row M6: String.prototype.search with RegExp.prototype[%Symbol.search%] deleted, and with an own %Symbol.search% of undefined or null; Broiler.JS answers 1, the index of its direct value.Match (BuiltIns/String/JSStringPrototype.Search.cs), where the specification throws a TypeError or answers -1; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0081); answered by SJL-11.5, the specification's path (decision D20)
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-string.prototype.search spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-regexp.prototype-%symbol.search% spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-regexpcreate
script: delete RegExp.prototype[Symbol.search]; "abc".search(/b/)
note: correspondence row M6: with RegExp.prototype[%Symbol.search%] deleted, search creates a RegExp from the argument and Invokes its %Symbol.search%, which is undefined; read from the clauses (the match itself is regexpref's where one runs)
since: 31

